1
00:00:04,662 --> 00:00:12,872
Close the books — Operations ▸ Accounting — Every visit, claim and payment lands in the ledger. This is where you check that it did.

2
00:00:18,428 --> 00:00:27,379
Operations ▸ Accounting opens on four numbers: what you are owed, what you owe, cash, and anything unposted.

3
00:00:27,379 --> 00:00:34,548
Module Integrations is the important part — these accounts are wired to claims, billing and payments.

4
00:00:34,548 --> 00:00:46,294
Which means the ledger fills itself in. Your job here is to check it, not to type it again.

5
00:00:46,294 --> 00:00:54,897
The chart of accounts is the shape of the books: assets, liabilities, equity, revenue, expense.

6
00:00:54,897 --> 00:01:05,751
The ones marked as system accounts are the ones other modules post into — leave those alone.

7
00:01:05,751 --> 00:01:13,923
The journal is every entry, with what created it: a remittance, a supplier invoice, or someone here by hand.

8
00:01:13,923 --> 00:01:24,882
A draft changes no balance. Only posting does — which is why the draft count is on the overview.

9
00:01:24,882 --> 00:01:36,344
Posted. Debits and credits balance, or the entry would not have been allowed to post at all.

10
00:01:36,344 --> 00:01:44,133
Receivables is what has not been paid yet, bucketed by how late it is — current, thirty days, sixty.

11
00:01:44,133 --> 00:01:56,771
Insurance and patient balances sit side by side, so chasing work can be sorted by age rather than by guess.

12
00:01:56,771 --> 00:02:09,018
Payables is the other direction — supplier invoices, including the ones raised by receiving stock.

13
00:02:09,018 --> 00:02:16,383
Reconciliation is the honest check: the bank’s balance against ours, and the difference between them.

14
00:02:16,383 --> 00:02:31,932
A non-zero discrepancy is the whole point of the screen — it is a thing to explain before you close the month.

15
00:02:31,932 --> 00:02:43,470
Statements close the loop with the payer or the patient: opening balance, charges, payments, what is left.

16
00:02:43,470 --> 00:02:51,121
Sent, and marked as sent. The books are closed, and every number on them can be traced back to a visit.

17
00:02:52,746 --> 00:03:06,626
What you just did

18
00:03:07,232 --> 00:03:16,232
